<title>FRANCE: AXA-UAP DENIES PROVISIONS REPORT.</title>
<headline>AXA-UAP DENIES PROVISIONS REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer AXA-UAP said on Wednesday that there was no truth to a French newspaper report that it would have to provision two billion francs a year for several years for its unit UAP-Vie.</p>
<p>&quot;The group Axa-UAP wishes to state that the information contained in the (Le Figaro) is without foundation,&quot; said the company in a statement.</p>
<p>The newspaper had said that the insurer would need to make the provisions to plug a structural deficit in part of UAP-Vie's portfolio.</p>
<p>Axa and UAP's merger took effect at the start of the year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 nim/pmc</p>
